\section{Reflection}{
\p{\strong{What went well today?} I officially implemented the Huberman routine. Specifically, fasting (I have protein shake but in spirt) does seem to really help me focus. I get VERY hungry before the end of the second block, so I need to find a solution for that. Overall, focus was pretty good but mainly on understanding [DDO](foxMultiLevelDiscoveryDeep2017)}
\p{\strong{What went bad today?} I still crashed post-lunch. I think this may be inevitable and seems commonplace throughout corporate America. It seems this may be a diet issue. Unfortunately, avoiding carbs for focus directly interferes with my need for carbs for exercise. I am unsure how to resolve this. I got my Anki done during the crash, but I still have not been able to do any exploratory reading to add to it. I think when reading I still do too much switching between reading and taking notes. I should really try to stay disciplined in first reading, then trying to dump without the source material. Any questions I have I should write down and move on, then look back for answers at the end.}
